Stable guest ABI for recompiled code, so everyday rebuilds stay incremental. ps2_guest_abi.h holds R5900Context, the
address map (moved from ps2_memory.h into runtime/ps2_address.h) and ps2_guest:: free functions that forward to the
PS2Runtime methods generated code calls (dispatchGuestBranch, eeCheckpointDue, Load/Store, handleSyscall, ...);
PS2Runtime is an incomplete type there. The emitters call ps2_guest::X(runtime, ...) instead of runtime->X(...), and
each generated function file declares only the functions it calls directly instead of including
ps2_recompiled_functions.h. Edits to PS2Runtime or the runtime subsystems and regenerations that add or remove a
function no longer rebuild the generated code. register_functions.cpp is built outside unity batches at -O0 -g0.
Runner unity builds and the runner PCH now default to OFF: unity batches shift when a function is added, and ccache
never hits on CMake's GCC PCH (the .gch command includes the previous, non-reproducible .gch).

